Communication Directions	
North-South (External Inbound):	
1	Internet Client
	Internet Gateway
	AWS ALB
	(Public HTTPS).
2	AWS ALB
	K8s Ingress Controller
	(NodePort/TargetGroup routing).
3	Ingress Controller
	Frontend Service
	Frontend Pods
	.
East-West (Internal Cluster Traffic):	
1	Frontend Pods
	Backend Service (ClusterIP)
	Backend Pods
	(Internal REST/gRPC API calls).
2	Backend Pods
	/
	Worker Pods
	read settings from
	ConfigMaps
	and credentials from
	Secrets
	inside the
	my-app
	namespace.
EKS to External AWS Services:	
1	Database:
	Backend
	&
	Worker Pods
	RDS Instance
	via private database endpoints over Port 5432 (PostgreSQL) or 3306 (MySQL).
2	Object Storage:
	Backend
	&
	Worker Pods
	Amazon S3
	API calls using IAM credentials provided automatically by the pod's
	ServiceAccount
	.
3	Messaging:
	Backend Pods
	Amazon SNS
	to publish event notifications using the pod's
	ServiceAccount